title: Cross-cutting concepts
---

# Cross-cutting concepts

{% callout type="info" title="About this chapter" %}
This chapter collects rules and solution approaches that apply to several building blocks – such as security, error handling, logging or persistence. This keeps the building block view free of repetition.
{% /callout %}

## Security

Users sign in through the central identity provider (OpenID Connect). Each service validates access tokens and roles itself; there is no trusted zone inside the cluster ("zero trust").

## Data protection

{% callout type="warning" title="Personal data" %}
Position data allows conclusions about individual drivers. After 90 days it is aggregated at vehicle level and the raw data is deleted.
{% /callout %}

## Further concepts

{% details title="Logging and monitoring" %}
All services write structured logs (JSON) and metrics in OpenTelemetry format. Alert thresholds for each service are kept in the repository.
{% /details %}

{% details title="Error handling" %}
Events that still fail after three attempts are moved to a dead-letter queue and shown on the operations dashboard.
{% /details %}

{% details title="Internationalization" %}
The user interfaces are available in English and Spanish. Texts are kept in resource files; dates and numbers follow the user's language setting.
{% /details %}
